;; tags: mem-ops, loads, sign-extend
;; expect: -56
;; Signed byte load. Exercises LDRSB Xd, [Xn] -- sign-extends the byte
;; into all 64 bits (x86: MOVSX r64, BYTE PTR [reg]). The byte 0xC8
;; (== 200 unsigned) prints as -56 once sign-extended into an int.
;; Pair this with 21-mem-load8u.gc: same byte, opposite sign-extension
;; policy. Mixing the two up is the classic load-size codegen bug.
(defun main ()
  (let ((buf (new 'stack-no-clear 'array int8 1)))
    (set! (-> buf 0) (the int8 -56))
    (format #t "~D~%" (-> buf 0))))
